// Inputs that must produce a QUESTION, not a guess (architecture §3.5).
// Each case names the ambiguity KIND the engine has to raise. `ambiguityKinds`
// is a SUBSET assertion — the engine may legitimately add more questions, but it
// may never drop the one named here.
//
// ALL TEXT IS FABRICATED. `ctx` selects a fixture from runner.mjs:
//   one_household  — five distinct accounts, one household
//   two_households — same accounts, TWO households (household is always asked)
//   hdfc_twice     — two accounts that the alias "hdfc" matches equally
{"id":"amb-household-always","bucket":"ambiguous","ctx":"two_households","text":"850 groceries hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["household"],"minOptions":2},"note":"LOCKED product decision: household is asked whenever there is more than one, even when everything else resolved cleanly. Misfiling business vs personal is tax-visible and invisible to the user afterwards."}
{"id":"amb-household-obvious-still-asks","bucket":"ambiguous","ctx":"two_households","text":"spent 1200 on rent from icici","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["household"],"minOptions":2},"note":"A 95%-obvious personal spend gets asked too. There is deliberately no `likely household` heuristic."}
{"id":"amb-household-transfer","bucket":"ambiguous","ctx":"two_households","text":"moved 5000 from cash to hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["household"],"minOptions":2},"note":"Holds for neutral rows as well — a transfer inside the wrong household is still wrong."}
{"id":"amb-alias-two-accounts","bucket":"ambiguous","ctx":"hdfc_twice","text":"850 groceries hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["account"],"minOptions":2},"note":"Two accounts match `hdfc` equally. Picking the first would be a coin flip on the user's money — resolver rule 2."}
{"id":"amb-alias-two-accounts-verb","bucket":"ambiguous","ctx":"hdfc_twice","text":"spent 2400 from hdfc on shopping","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["account"],"minOptions":2},"note":"Same tie reached through the explicit `from` slot rather than the trailing-token heuristic."}
{"id":"amb-no-account-named","bucket":"ambiguous","text":"450 coffee","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["account"],"minOptions":2,"candidate":{"amount":450,"category_id":"food_dining"}},"note":"Nothing was said about an account, so the full list IS the useful option set (capped at 4)."}
{"id":"amb-polarity-both-verbs","bucket":"ambiguous","text":"paid 500 and received 200 from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["polarity"],"minOptions":2,"issues":["polarity_conflict"]},"note":"Both a debit and a credit verb are present. The grammar takes the type from the leading verb but leaves direction UNSET, and the validator degrades — asking is the whole point of §3.5 polarity."}
{"id":"amb-category-tie","bucket":"ambiguous","text":"1500 apollo policy from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["category"],"minOptions":2},"note":"apollo (health) and policy (insurance) are the same keyword length, so neither is more specific. A tie is a genuine 50/50 and must be asked, not resolved first-wins."}
{"id":"amb-card-three-way","bucket":"ambiguous","safety":true,"text":"1200 on kotak credit card","expect":{"outcome":"ask","ambiguityKinds":["txn_type"],"minOptions":2,"candidate":{"amount":1200,"account_alias":"Kotak Credit Card"}},"note":"BUG C, not a gap. This is the architecture's flagship §3.5 example (the `1200 amex` three-way: spend on the card / pay the card bill / transfer to the card). ambiguity.ts implements cardTxnTypeAmbiguity() and gates it on AmbiguityContext.hasCardAccountMatch — which pipeline.ts NEVER SETS when it builds the context. The branch is unreachable, so the pipeline WRITES silently instead of asking. Left SCORED and marked safety."}
